      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, thanks for seeing me. Um, I came in because... well, I'm a high school teacher, and I've just been really struggling to get through my work lately. Like, I can sit down with a stack of essays or a curriculum document, fully intending to get it all done. I'll have my coffee, my desk is clear... actually, I just got this new desk from IKEA last weekend. It's one of those adjustable standing desks? I thought maybe standing up would help me work better because sitting all day is supposed to be terrible for your posture anyway. My brother-in-law has one and he swears by it, though he works in tech, so he's always just typing code or whatever. \n\nAnyway, sorry, what was I saying? Oh, right. So I'll sit—or stand—at the desk with the essays, and within like ten minutes, I realize I’ve just been staring at the exact same page. I'll be thinking about three completely different things, like whether I remembered to switch the laundry or if my car needs an oil change, and I'm barely taking in a single word of what's actually right in front of me.",
