    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Did you experience similar difficulties with attention or focus when you were a child or teenager?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually, I did. Even way back in primary school, my report cards always said the exact same things. Like, \"bright but careless,\" or \"doesn't finish work unless closely supervised.\" My parents were constantly finding these crumpled up worksheets at the bottom of my backpack that I just completely forgot to turn in. Which is funny, because now I'm the one handing out the worksheets. I try to make them interesting, you know? Like last week we were doing this unit on the Industrial Revolution, and I found this really cool interactive map online that shows how the factories spread across Europe. The kids actually seemed to like it, well, most of them. There's always a few who just want to play games on their Chromebooks. I mean, I get it, those Chromebooks are pretty distracting. I had to confiscate three of them just on Tuesday. \n\nBut yeah, the focus thing... it's definitely not a new problem for me. It's just always been there, I guess.",
