    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel physically restless, fidgety, or like you have trouble sitting still for long periods?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, not really? I mean, I don't feel like I have to be running around or anything. I can sit still just fine. Well, mostly. I might bounce my leg a bit when I'm grading, but I think everyone does that, right? It's just a habit. Kind of like how I always have to have a pen in my hand when I'm teaching. Not even to write with, just to hold. I lost my favorite pen last week, actually. It was this really nice metal one my sister got me for my birthday. She's always getting me these fancy office supplies because she thinks it'll help me stay organized. She got me this leather planner last year that I used for exactly three days before I lost it in my car. My car is a total mess right now, to be honest. I keep meaning to clean it out, but by the time I get home from school, I'm just so drained. \n\nBut no, to answer your question, I don't really feel physically restless. It's more just... my brain won't stay put, you know?",
